type: diagnosis
title: CielAiRouter 500 reported crash/background-move/duplicate-session chain — verification and status-faithful transport fix
status: diagnosed-fixed-pending-release
date: 2026-11-04
---

# Report under verification (user)
"지금으로 써 알려진 레포트에 의하면 error 500같은 ciel ai router 단예세ㅓ 에러가 나오면 조용히 ciel runtime이 크래시되면서 claude는 백그라운드로 자동으로 이전되고. 사용자가 새로 실행하면 새로운 세션이 나와서 중복세션등이 생기는 문제로 알려져잇어"

Chain to verify: (1) CielAiRouter-side HTTP 500 → (2) ciel-runtime quietly crashes → (3) Claude automatically moves to background → (4) user re-launches → (5) a new duplicate session instead of resuming.

# Evidence collected

## Prody router log (goal 34 host, ssh sjglobal@100.64.0.12 -p 1004, instance 9592-c53b7c787223)
- `anthropic_route_error` hits = 22. Every one is a **local status=500 generated after an upstream transport `RuntimeError`** (Errno 10053 / WinError 10054 / 10061 / 11001) or transient-retry exhaustion — not an observed CielAiRouter HTTP 500 relayed downstream.
- Previous journal (2026-10-28 gateway-error-envelope) independently confirms the mechanism: "upstream_retry wraps them in RuntimeError, then the local route responds HTTP500. This is not evidence that an HTTP500 response came from CielAiRouter."
- Shutdown/traceback greps did not establish a router-process crash; the 218 `Traceback` lines are per-request handler traces (socketserver `process_request_thread`/`finish_request`), and the log's first line is the router starting on 127.0.0.1:9592.

## Code paths (this worktree)
- `claude_router.py:698-722` preserves an upstream `HTTPError` status/body verbatim (HTTPError path).
- Non-HTTP exceptions fell into the generic boundary and were written as a **blind local 500** (`try_write_json(..., 500)`), erasing transport identity (10053/10054 reset vs timeout vs refused).
- `upstream_retry.py` wrapped final `URLError`/`OSError` failures in bare `RuntimeError("upstream ... request failed ...")` in all three entry points, discarding the structured failure. `upstream_error_policy.py` already classifies these as `UpstreamFailure` (502, or 504 for real timeouts; `_transport_status:187-193`).
- Router process: `ciel_runtime.py:3007` wires `ThreadingHTTPServer`; `router_server_runtime.py:80` `serve_forever()`. A route exception is a request-thread failure. No `sys.exit`/`os._exit`/terminate/kill exists in `claude_router.py`, `router_server_context.py`, or `router_client_lifecycle.py`. The launcher's SystemExit uses in `cli_dispatch.py:195-744` are argument-usage validation only.
- `router_client_lifecycle.py` `RouterLifetime.stop_if_idle` only stops the **router** after the last client lease releases (`stop_if_idle("claude_exit")`) — it cannot move Claude to background.

## Prody transcripts (duplicate condition)
- Same project (`C--ProgramData-aap-win-sandboxes-u41-home-prody-ai`) holds multiple transcripts, all attach/bg-associated:
  - `f7a53287` — long existing bg session, created 2026-11-03 20:56, `sessionKind=bg` throughout.
  - `543686ba` — created 2026-11-04 12:04:46 (-08:00), first user message is `attach`, first bg info at 20:03:39Z; logs `Backgrounding after the current tool finishes…` then `Backgrounding cancelled ? the turn was stopped.`
  - `c0d8ddd4` — same `attach` first message; `sessionKind` empty on first info line, bg marker later.
  - `3c31fbc4…orphaned-…jsonl` — created in the same 12:04:46 window, `sessionKind=bg`.
- `sessionKind=bg` and `Backgrounding…` lines are Claude Code's own background-session state. Nothing in ciel-runtime writes them.
- `session_resume_last.py:47-83`: ciel-runtime's resume gate only checks that **some** `*.jsonl` exists in the folder and then adds `--continue`; it cannot name or attach a specific live Claude bg session. So when Claude starts (or misroutes to) a new transcript instead of attaching the intended bg session, ciel-runtime has no signal to prevent the duplicate.

# Verdict (confirmed vs unproven)
- ✅ **Refuted as stated**: an upstream 500 → ciel-runtime process crash → automatic background move. No code path and no field evidence supports the first two links. The router is threaded; route failures are per-request.
- ✅ **Real defect found and fixed**: final upstream transport failures lost their identity and became a local naked 500. This is the client-visible "ciel-runtime 500" the report most plausibly points at — the client sees an opaque 500 from the local router, not a faithful 502/504 gateway error.
- ✅ **Duplicate condition localized**: same-cwd multiple bg transcripts + folder-level `--continue` gate. The duplicate is produced by Claude's attach/new choice when session identity is not pinned; ciel-runtime cannot currently prevent it, and a hard launch block would be speculative without a stable ciel-runtime-owned live-session registry.
- 🟡 **Unproven, left open**: why Prody's router MCP disconnected and why Walkie SSE routed to temp session 543686ba (goal 34 open question). No disconnect line in router.log or transcript tails; the f7a53287 tail shows work continuing (gates `wg-mw2k003g-4`) and then `ECONNREFUSED`/MCP-missing reconciliation notes, then end of file — no third session-start record. The 664a228b tail (`continued-in`, cost-state) is a different cwd-holding conversation and was not connected to the reported chain.

# Fix applied (worktree, not yet released)
- `upstream_retry.py`: in `post_json_with_rate_retry`, `open_provider_request_with_key_retry`, and `open_openai_stream_with_rate_retry`, a final transport error is now converted with `UpstreamFailure.from_transport_error(...)` when it is a real upstream transport failure (502, or 504 for timeouts); non-transport bugs keep the existing generic `RuntimeError`, so programming errors still surface unchanged.
- `claude_router.py` generic exception boundary: if the exception is (or converts from transport into) an `UpstreamFailure`, the router logs `anthropic_route_error … status=<failure.status_code>` and writes `failure.anthropic_payload()` with that status; otherwise the pre-existing local 500 remains for genuine local defects.
- `tests/test_upstream_retry.py`: gateway-boundary expectations updated from exact `RuntimeError` type to `RuntimeError` instance (UpstreamFailure **is** a RuntimeError subclass; the stricter claim is preserved via `isinstance`).
- Scope boundary: observed upstream HTTP 500 bodies still classify as `upstream_error`/500 by the existing observed-status logic; only the transport-to-naked-500 erasure is removed. No launch-time duplicate guard was added (see verdict).

# Verification
- `python -m pytest tests/test_upstream_retry.py tests/test_upstream_failure_model.py tests/test_initial_stream_retry.py tests/test_router_client_lifecycle.py tests/test_unattended_restart.py -q` → **89 passed, 76 subtests passed**.
- `python -m pytest tests/test_router_server_runtime.py -q` → 3 passed, 2 subtests passed.
- `git diff --check` clean. Diff: `ciel_runtime_support/claude_router.py` +15, `ciel_runtime_support/upstream_retry.py` +9, `tests/test_upstream_retry.py` 4 changed lines.

# Release boundary
- Worktree only. Not committed, not pushed, no nightly, no local snapshot install. Running routers/sessions were not restarted.
- Prody/Kobi field updates remain separate approvals; nothing was changed on .12/.14 in this goal beyond the read-only probes above.
